"archetype":"regular","unseen":false,"pinned":false,"unpinned":null,"excerpt":"Where does the bug appear (feature/product)?\nGrok Bot \nDescribe the Bug\nNew Grok Bot installation, v0.36.0, macOS. Setup fails with “Can’t reach your computer”. Tested normal Wi-Fi and iPhone hotspot on a separate mobile\u0026hellip;","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"bookmarked":null,"liked":null,"thumbnails":null,"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"like_count":0,"views":58,"category_id":6,"featured_link":null,"op_like_count":0,"has_accepted_answer":false,"posters":[{"extras":null,"description":"Original Poster","user":{"id":135966,"username":"ALIN_FARAH","name":"ALIN FARAH","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/ecd19e/{size}.png","trust_level":0}},{"extras":"latest","description":"Most Recent Poster","user":{"id":87436,"username":"Colin","name":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_group_id":42,"primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":3}}]}],"summarizable":false,"has_cached_summary":false,"valid_reactions":["heart","+1","crossed_fingers","clap","laughing","open_mouth","confetti_ball","hugs","heavy_plus_sign","heart_eyes","sunglasses","cursor"],"accepted_answers":[{"id":487512,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:13:22.692Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report. First off, it’s not your network, browser, or VPN, so there’s no point changing those next. This isn’t a setup issue on your side.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat’s happening: on a new account, the Privacy Mode choice hasn’t been explicitly saved yet, and Grok Bot needs that saved choice to connect to its computer. Until it’s set, every connection attempt gets rejected, and Retry / Recover / Reset can’t move forward either.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow to unblock it:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn your browser, go to \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com/dashboard\"\u003ecursor.com/dashboard\u003c/a\u003e and sign in with the same account you’re using in Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Settings and find the Privacy section.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSelect Privacy Mode, not the Legacy option, keep data sharing turned off, and confirm.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot on your Mac with \u003ccode\u003eCmd+Q\u003c/code\u003e, then open it again.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf it still says Connecting after a minute, click Retry once.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf it’s still stuck after a couple minutes, use Reset once. Since the account is new, there’s nothing important on the computer to lose, and Reset should complete now.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour iPhone will sync automatically as soon as the Mac connects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf it still doesn’t work after this, send the attempt time with your timezone and we’ll dig in further. This is a known issue we’re tracking.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"topic_id":171170,"url":"/t/grok-bot-macos-persistent-cant-reach-your-computer/171170/8","accepter_name":"Dean Rie","accepter_username":"deanrie"}],"has_accepted_answer":true,"can_create_shared_issue":false,"shared_issue_visible":false,"can_vote":false,"vote_count":0,"user_voted":false,"discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_id":null,"discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_url":"https://your-url.zendesk.com/agent/tickets/","details":{"can_edit":false,"notification_level":1,"participants":[{"id":137029,"username":"Teddy1","name":"Teddy","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/71c47a/{size}.png","post_count":2,"pri